# Maskfish contains code from other projects, whose authors keep their copyright
# on the code they wrote:
#
# - jqe, from which the engine (src/), the referee (tools/native/, tools/jieqi/),
#   the tools and the record reading of the trainer (train/records.py) are
#   derived;
# - AB-JChess, from which the network evaluator (src/hnn/), the network packer
#   (tools/hnn/) and the trainer (train/) are derived; it contains code derived
#   from Pikafish and Stockfish;
# - Pikafish and Stockfish, through AB-JChess (among them the signed LEB128
#   container of the network files, src/hnn/jqnz.h).
#
#   Copyright (C) 2026 The Maskfish authors
#   Copyright (C) 2026 Devin O'Keefe (jqe)
#   Copyright (C) The AB-JChess authors
#   Copyright (C) 2004-2023 The Pikafish developers
#   Copyright (C) 2004-2025 The Stockfish developers
#
# Maskfish is released under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later
# (see Copying.txt), as are AB-JChess, Pikafish and Stockfish. jqe is released
# under the MIT License, whose notice is reproduced at the end of this file.
#
# Maskfish's default network is the network of AB-JChess's release 20261031
# (abjchess-20261030.nnue) and the nets trained from it.
#
# Maskfish also follows other projects, without containing their code:
#
# - the rules are those of Jieqi as played on the Tiantian app, with the
#   conventions of Pikafish's Jieqi branch where the published rules are
#   silent; the FEN and move notation of its UCI protocol (face-down pieces,
#   urns, revealed and captured identities in the move tokens, the order
#   R A C P N B of the urns, the x / X suffix of a lone reveal) is that of
#   Pikafish's Jieqi branch;
# - the local test server (fishtest/) is modelled on the fishtest of Stockfish
#   and Pikafish: the pentanomial generalized SPRT, normalized Elo, the SPSA
#   gains and parameter format (name,start,min,max,c_end,r_end, defaults of
#   Stockfish's TUNE()), the presets of the test form and the nn-<sha256>
#   network names; tools/sprt.py uses the same generalized SPRT;
# - tests/reprosearch.py follows Stockfish's tests/reprosearch.sh.

